(*
FloatSmokeNode — exercises the boxed-Float path on a target with NO FPU.

The C6 ISA is rv32imac_zicsr: no 'f', no 'd' extension, so every float
operation here is a soft-float libcall. This node exists because TimerNode
(the bench gate) boxes no floats at all, leaving both soft-float AND the
float-arena knobs (OEVM_FLOAT_ARENA_SLAB_CELLS / _SLAB_BUDGET) completely
unexercised on this target.

The arena knobs are carried over from Xtensa on the PREDICTION that struct
Float stays 16 B under the RISC-V ilp32 ABI. Task 4 confirmed the size, but
size is not the same as the arena behaving correctly under churn.

TERM COUNT IS LOAD-BEARING — do not lower it. gc.c float_alloc()'s reclaim
path (gc_collect() + float_sweep() refilling float_freelist) fires only when
float_slab_count >= OEVM_FLOAT_ARENA_SLAB_BUDGET (4), i.e. after
4 * OEVM_FLOAT_ARENA_SLAB_CELLS = 2048 cells. Each iteration boxes THREE
Floats (i asFloat, the division result, the addition result — dispatch.c
PRIM_asFloat and vm.c's Float branches of OP_DIV/OP_ADD all call float_alloc
unconditionally), so 1001 iterations box ~3003 cells ≈ 5.9 slabs and cross
that threshold comfortably. An earlier 200-iteration version boxed ~600 cells,
crossed the slab boundary only once (1->2) and NEVER reached the budget — it
exercised slab growth but not reclaim, which is the mechanism the
"VM Float Arena Error: Out of Memory" risk actually lives in.

Grants no capability, so no `net:` header. No radio, no timer, no hardware.

Sum is Sum_{i=1..1001} i/3 = (1001*1002/2)/3 = 501501/3 = 167167.0 exactly.
1001 is chosen so N(N+1)/2 is divisible by 3 AND the term-by-term IEEE-754
accumulation lands bit-exact on that integer (verified in double precision,
not assumed — an inexact sum would make the expect: line format-dependent).
printString drops the trailing ".0", hence "float-smoke sum=167167" below. Confirmed against a host
run (nsl-tuvm/tools/run-one.py) rather than assumed: the brief's original
draft of this header listed only the final "float-smoke ok" line, which
under-specified the expect: block against run-one.py's exact-match semantics
(compare TimerNodeHost.nsl's two-line TIMER OK / CANCEL OK block) — every
println line the node emits must appear here, in order.
expect:
float-smoke sum=167167
float-smoke ok
*)
class FloatSmokeNode packageUsing: manifest = (
| private sum ::= 0.0 asFloat. |
) (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    1 to: 1001 do: [ :i | sum:: sum + (i asFloat / 3.0) ].
    ('float-smoke sum=', sum printString) println.
    'float-smoke ok' println.
    ^ 0
  )
) : (
)
